review_comments.body:
Rather than rebuilding a client (and pipeline) per request and re-applying the options in three places, derive these from the service client. It already carries the SAS query, the strip policy and the retry options, and the SDK escapes names the same way (`url.PathEscape` + `runtime.JoinPaths`, which keeps the query):

```go
func (az *Azure) getBlobClient(cntr, blb string) (*blob.Client, error) {
	return az.client.ServiceClient().NewContainerClient(cntr).NewBlobClient(blb), nil
}

func (az *Azure) getContainerClient(cntr string) (*container.Client, error) {
	return az.client.ServiceClient().NewContainerClient(cntr), nil
}

func (az *Azure) getBlockBlobClient(cntr, blb string) (*blockblob.Client, error) {
	return az.client.ServiceClient().NewContainerClient(cntr).NewBlockBlobClient(blb), nil
}
```

This makes the fix structural (a future helper can't forget the options), drops the manual `+"?"+az.sasToken` concatenation, and shares one pipeline (including the bearer-token cache with default credentials). The exported `azblobclient.ClientOptions()` is then not needed. Your new test and the full `backend/azure` suite pass with this change.
